course: dictionary
lesson: 10758
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word urn is a good example. «After a cremation the ashes are given to the family in an urn and may be buried, kept or scattered somewhere the person loved.» The clues are cremation and ashes, so this urn is a container for the ashes of a person who has died.
explain: An urn can also be a large metal container with a tap. Think about the place where you find it. At a school fete or in a church hall, an urn full of hot water is used to make and serve tea or coffee. The setting tells you which meaning is right.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning and reading the sentence again. Does «a tall vase with a lid» make sense? Does «a metal container with a tap» make sense? The meaning that fits every clue in the sentence is the right one.
fact: An urn is a tall vase, often with a lid.
fact: An urn can hold the ashes of a person who has died.
fact: A tea urn is a large metal container with a tap, used for making and serving tea or coffee.
fact: Phrases with urn include «a tea urn» and «an urn of ashes».
fact: The same word can have different meanings, so always read the clues around it.
exercise: «After a cremation the ashes are given to the family in an urn.» What is an urn in this sentence? | A large metal container with a tap for hot drinks | A bunch of flowers | *A tall vase, often with a lid, that holds ashes | A kind of bread
exercise: At the school fete, Mrs Patel fills the urn with hot water. What is the urn? | A kind of cake | A stone in the garden | A tall vase with a lid, for decoration | *A large metal container with a tap, for hot drinks
exercise: «After a cremation the ashes are given to the family in an urn.» Which word is the best clue that the urn holds a person's ashes? | given | *cremation | after | family
test: «The urn in the hall kept the water hot for the church teas.» What does urn mean here? | A cup and saucer | *A large metal container with a tap, for making and serving tea | A tin of biscuits | A tall vase with a lid
test: «She kept her grandad's ashes in a plain urn on the shelf.» What does urn mean here? | *A tall vase, often with a lid, used to hold ashes | A type of plant | A kind of cake | A metal container with a tap for hot drinks
exam: «The urn at the fete was full of hot tea.» Which meaning fits this sentence, and which clue tells you? | A bunch of flowers, because of tea | A tall vase with a lid, because of fete | *A large metal container with a tap, because of fete, hot and tea | An urn of ashes, because of hot
